    "turn_idx": 29,
    "turn_text": "As a country, we need to do something. We've got to get rid of Obamacare because it's failed and continues to get worse for people. I think like most everybody in the district, we're disappointed that something didn't happen. The Senate couldn't come to an agreement on any version of repeal back in July. I don't know if they will take it up for sure when they get back. I do know there's some hearings being scheduled that first week committee hearings anyway on the Senate side. I'd be surprised really if they do take it up because I just don't see a path based on where they ended. Now I'm not the best expert on the Senate. I'm still learning some of the things in the",
