    "turn_text": "forget the terminology that Josh uses mostly with his practice, but you see more and more of those. Several across the state, I mean, I know there's a set up in Topeka as well. It's one of those things that actually kind of takes healthcare from the way it's been for the last 50, 60 years back into the same approach that you do for anything else. You know, when we think about car insurance, we don't use our car insurance when we have to replace the tires or have to replace the brakes or to get the oil changed. but we've treated our health insurance as if it should pay for everything. So, you know, one of these other approaches kind of tends to get how do we provide health care and then health insurance is on the side that helps with some of those catastrophic things. So I think there's some value there. Things like health savings accounts that are available now, particularly if you're with an employer who offers that and you get a high deductible insurance policy, gives you some opportunity to set aside some money that you can then pay for those doctor visits and prescriptions and other things that seem to make a lot of sense in that regard. One of",
