    "turn_idx": 37,
    "turn_text": "Most of the major programs at the federal level have to be reauthorized every few years. And part of that goes back to, you don't know what kind of rules change, what kind of rural conditions might change, how you want to set the policy for that. FAA is one of those things that is coming up for reauthorization this year as of the end of September. And as part of that, some members of Congress are talking about what they're calling privatization for the air traffic controllers and are attaching that to the authorization for the FAA. And the problem with that air traffic control, what they're calling privatization is really it's a give away of the assets that the federal government has built up over the years in setting up that air traffic control system and making sure that that worked for us across the country. Giving that to, I call it a quasi-government agency, but really it's a standalone entity, sort of like the CFPB",
